comments.message:
I wrote this little program:
```
boost::urls::url testUrl = boost::urls::format("/foo/bar/baz");
boost::urls::url another = boost::urls::format("{}/bod", testUrl);
std::cerr << testUrl << "\n";
std::cerr << another << "\n";
```

and this was the output:

```
/foo/bar/baz
/foo/bar/baz/bod
```

It seems to work as expected?

Probably still best to use the utility function, considering that it's more clear that's the behavior.  I'd be curious what

```
boost::urls::url testUrl = boost::urls::format("http://1.1.1.1/foo/bar/baz");
boost::urls::url another = boost::urls::format("http://http://1.1.1.1/{}/bod", testUrl);
std::cerr << testUrl << "\n";
std::cerr << another << "\n";
```

Does.  I'll have to try that tomorrow.
